#: ../../source/got_readme.md:82
msgid ""
"It's a `GET` request by default, but can be changed by using different "
"methods or in the `options`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/got_readme.md:84
msgid "got(url, [options])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/got_readme.md:86
msgid ""
"Returns a Promise for a `response` object with a `body` property, a `url`"
" property with the request URL or the final URL after redirects, and a "
"`requestUrl` property with the original request URL."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/got_readme.md:88
msgid ""
"The response object will normally be a [Node.js HTTP response "
"stream](https://nodejs.org/api/http.html#http_class_http_incomingmessage),"
" however if returned from the cache it will be a [responselike "
"object](https://github.com/lukechilds/responselike) which behaves in the "
"same way."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/got_readme.md:90
msgid ""
"The response will also have a `fromCache` property set with a boolean "
"value."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/got_readme.md:92
msgid "url"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/got_readme.md:94
msgid "Type: `string` `Object`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/got_readme.md:96
msgid ""
"The URL to request as simple string, a [`http.request` "
"options](https://nodejs.org/api/http.html#http_http_request_options_callback),"
" or a [WHATWG `URL`](https://nodejs.org/api/url.html#url_class_url)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/got_readme.md:98
msgid "Properties from `options` will override properties in the parsed `url`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/got_readme.md:100
msgid "If no protocol is specified, it will default to `https`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/got_readme.md:102
msgid "options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/got_readme.md:104
msgid "Type: `Object`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/got_readme.md:106
msgid ""
"Any of the "
"[`http.request`](http://nodejs.org/api/http.html#http_http_request_options_callback)"
" options."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/got_readme.md:108
msgid "stream"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/got_readme.md:110 ../../source/got_readme.md:136
#: ../../source/got_readme.md:147 ../../source/got_readme.md:211
msgid "Type: `boolean`<br> Default: `false`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/got_readme.md:113
msgid ""
"Returns a `Stream` instead of a `Promise`. This is equivalent to calling "
"`got.stream(url, [options])`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/got_readme.md:115
msgid "body"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/got_readme.md:117
msgid "Type: `string` `Buffer` `stream.Readable`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/got_readme.md:119 ../../source/got_readme.md:139
#: ../../source/got_readme.md:150
msgid "*This is mutually exclusive with stream mode.*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/got_readme.md:121
msgid "Body that will be sent with a `POST` request."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/got_readme.md:123
msgid ""
"If present in `options` and `options.method` is not set, `options.method`"
" will be set to `POST`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/got_readme.md:125
msgid ""
"If `content-length` or `transfer-encoding` is not set in "
"`options.headers` and `body` is a string or buffer, `content-length` will"
" be set to the body length."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/got_readme.md:127
msgid "encoding"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/got_readme.md:129
msgid "Type: `string` `null`<br> Default: `'utf8'`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/got_readme.md:132
msgid ""
"[Encoding](https://nodejs.org/api/buffer.html#buffer_buffers_and_character_encodings)"
" to be used on `setEncoding` of the response data. If `null`, the body is"
" returned as a [`Buffer`](https://nodejs.org/api/buffer.html) (binary "
"data)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/got_readme.md:134
msgid "form"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/got_readme.md:141
msgid ""
"If set to `true` and `Content-Type` header is not set, it will be set to "
"`application/x-www-form-urlencoded`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/got_readme.md:143 ../../source/got_readme.md:156
msgid "`body` must be a plain object or array and will be stringified."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/got_readme.md:145
msgid "json"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/got_readme.md:152
msgid ""
"If set to `true` and `Content-Type` header is not set, it will be set to "
"`application/json`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/got_readme.md:154
msgid ""
"Parse response body with `JSON.parse` and set `accept` header to "
"`application/json`. If used in conjunction with the `form` option, the "
"`body` will the stringified as querystring and the response parsed as "
"JSON."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/got_readme.md:158
msgid "query"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/got_readme.md:160
msgid "Type: `string` `Object`<br>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/got_readme.md:162
msgid ""
"Query string object that will be added to the request URL. This will "
"override the query string in `url`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/got_readme.md:164
msgid "timeout"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/got_readme.md:166
msgid "Type: `number` `Object`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/got_readme.md:168
msgid ""
"Milliseconds to wait for the server to end the response before aborting "
"request with `ETIMEDOUT` error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/got_readme.md:170
msgid ""
"This also accepts an object with separate `connect`, `socket`, and "
"`request` fields for connection, socket, and entire request timeouts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/got_readme.md:172
msgid "retries"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/got_readme.md:174
msgid "Type: `number` `Function`<br> Default: `2`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/got_readme.md:177
msgid ""
"Number of request retries when network errors happens. Delays between "
"retries counts with function `1000 * Math.pow(2, retry) + Math.random() *"
" 100`, where `retry` is attempt number (starts from 0)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/got_readme.md:179
msgid ""
"Option accepts `function` with `retry` and `error` arguments. Function "
"must return delay in milliseconds (`0` return value cancels retry)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/got_readme.md:181
msgid ""
"**Note:** if `retries` is `number`, `ENOTFOUND` and `ENETUNREACH` error "
"will not be retried (see full list in [`is-retry-"
"allowed`](https://github.com/floatdrop/is-retry-"
"allowed/blob/master/index.js#L12) module)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/got_readme.md:183
msgid "followRedirect"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/got_readme.md:185 ../../source/got_readme.md:195
#: ../../source/got_readme.md:218
msgid "Type: `boolean`<br> Default: `true`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/got_readme.md:188
msgid "Defines if redirect responses should be followed automatically."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/got_readme.md:190
msgid ""
"Note that if a `303` is sent by the server in response to any request "
"type (`POST`, `DELETE`, etc.), got will automatically request the "
"resource pointed to in the location header via `GET`. This is in "
"accordance with [the "
"spec](https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc7231#section-6.4.4)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/got_readme.md:193
msgid "decompress"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/got_readme.md:198
msgid ""
"Decompress the response automatically. This will set the `accept-"
"encoding` header to `gzip, deflate` unless you set it yourself."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/got_readme.md:200
msgid ""
"If this is disabled, a compressed response is returned as a `Buffer`. "
"This may be useful if you want to handle decompression yourself or stream"
" the raw compressed data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/got_readme.md:202
msgid "cache"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/got_readme.md:204
msgid "Type: `Object`<br> Default: `false`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/got_readme.md:207
msgid "[Cache adapter instance](#cache-adapters) for storing cached data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/got_readme.md:209
msgid "useElectronNet"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/got_readme.md:214
msgid ""
"When used in Electron, Got will use "
"[`electron.net`](https://electronjs.org/docs/api/net/) instead of the "
"Node.js `http` module. According to the Electron docs, it should be fully"
" compatible, but it's not entirely. See "
"[#315](https://github.com/sindresorhus/got/issues/315)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/got_readme.md:216
msgid "throwHttpErrors"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/got_readme.md:221
msgid ""
"Determines if a `got.HTTPError` is thrown for error responses (non-2xx "
"status codes)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/got_readme.md:223
msgid ""
"If this is disabled, requests that encounter an error status code will be"
" resolved with the `response` instead of throwing. This may be useful if "
"you are checking for resource availability and are expecting error "
"responses."
msgstr ""

